sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/maynardsmith-war-of-attrition> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/TestableHypothesis>;
    dc:description "In contests settled by display, where the animal willing to persist longer wins and costs grow with time, the stable strategy is to choose a persistence time at random from an exponential distribution whose mean equals the resource value.";
    dc:source "John Maynard Smith (1974) The theory of games and the evolution of animal conflicts";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "War of attrition ESS";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(78)90304-1>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "with cost linear in time at unit rate and resource value V, the ESS persistence time has density p(x) = \\frac{1}{V} e^{-x/V}";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Assumptions: symmetric contests, cost linear in display time, no information about the opponent's choice. Formal status: proved (Maynard Smith 1974); existence and uniqueness in the generalized game proved by Bishop and Cannings (1978).";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hypothesisType> "model-theorem";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/proposedTest> "Record contest durations in a display-based contest system and test for an exponential distribution, with the mean scaling with experimentally varied resource value."
}
